" "q-42606/selection/ma-v1/2d13ba836f9b2ed4409bffcbec96265ab53c6f455ac0bad3148797e37f740a2e/4d3ad046e73a1d030f06c8476f66e1d035bdfc75dcc35dd43ef70c21a11428a7" "q-42606/selection/ma-v1/2d13ba836f9b2ed4409bffcbec96265ab53c6f455ac0bad3148797e37f740a2e/ec00f0eed55244876793fbff3a77cfc6fff76867757a7a234e0454a98b3f2620" "q-42606/selection/ma-v1/2d13ba836f9b2ed4409bffcbec96265ab53c6f455ac0bad3148797e37f740a2e/2e6e9bd7a12ccd0a8d0d03ba09011e6667d4eedc34e70770ddf971e25a459c5b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42606"] :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=15 \\\\ 2x-3y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=15 \\\\ 2x-3y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42606/selection/ma-v1/2d13ba836f9b2ed4409bffcbec96265ab53c6f455ac0bad3148797e37f740a2e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-42970/selection/1a848d5be822087af6896c4be520d427214b654be6fe556e4f3b04a8d1df3b05" :answer/id #uuid "82becbd4-494e-51ec-b394-8bedbea10379" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,7 & 13 \\\\ -5 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/